## 5. Syntax Error vs Runtime Error

| Feature | Syntax Error | Runtime Error |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Problem** | Problem with code structure/grammar | Problem while executing |
| **When it happens** | Happens during compilation/parsing | Happens during execution |
| **Execution state** | Normal execution doesn't start | Previous valid code may already have executed |
| **Example** | Missing `:` (`if x > 10`) | Divide by zero (`10 / 0`) |

> **Easy memory:** Syntax error = Python can't properly understand the code. Runtime error = Python understands the code, but something goes wrong while running it.

